<p class="status-info"><strong>Under maintenance.</strong> Friends’ packs will be added later once the online service is ready. Joining, browsing shared packs and updating group collections are currently disabled. Your local packs and saved group working copies remain editable.</p>
<AppDisclosure Open="true"><Header>@L["What is already built?"]</Header><ChildContent><p>The prototype includes invitation links/codes, an invited-group overview, shared collections, creator/editor credits and emoji reactions. It has been tested locally; it is not currently offered as a working online service in the app. Automatic syncing and personal phone–PC sync are still future work.</p></ChildContent></AppDisclosure>
<AppDisclosure><Header>@L["How invitations and visibility will work"]</Header><ChildContent><ol><li>Receive a limited-use group invitation link or code.</li><li>Review the group and approve joining with your chosen username.</li><li>Public means shared with invited group members. Private packs stay out of the group overview.</li></ol><p>First name, profile photo and device/storage statistics are not included in the prototype's group sharing.</p></ChildContent></AppDisclosure>
<AppDisclosure><Header>@L["Personal packs and group collections"]</Header><ChildContent><p>Personal public packs use an explicit upload action in the prototype. A group collection is edited through a private working copy in My Packs. Everyone in the group can contribute, then publish an updated revision. Conflicting updates retain your local work instead of silently replacing someone else's changes. Group badges identify these working copies; they do not mean the latest edits have been uploaded.</p></ChildContent></AppDisclosure>
<AppDisclosure><Header>@L["Credits, reactions and leaving"]</Header><ChildContent><p>Collections show who added a sticker and who last edited it. Emoji suggestions and a + picker provide reactions. Leaving a group revokes that device's membership and removes its personal publications; downloaded copies cannot be recalled. Maintenance mode does not delete previously uploaded files or revoke existing server credentials.</p></ChildContent></AppDisclosure>
